Dear John Wooten,

Over the past week, the Review and Selection Panel of the Stellar Community
Fund reviewed numerous submissions, but unfortunately your submission did
not meet the requirements
<https://stellarcommunityfund.gitbook.io/scf-handbook/scf-awards/official-r=
ules-for-submissions>
set by the selection panel at this time.

We will close your submission for now, but you'll be able to enter SCF with
a new submission two rounds from now (SCF#25 - Submission Deadline is March
10th, 2024)

Please find feedback on your submission from panel reviewers below.
Reviewer commented at 06.03.2024 22:16:
" Product & Ecosystem Value

   - There is a lot of information but not much related to what SCF
   reviewers care about: the Stellar integration. They haven't improved the=
ir
   submission based on the feedback from last time:
   - Unclear use of Stellar/ops mainly around Stock tokenization to allow
   for these benefits and the regulation implications.
   - Many of the deliverables aren't directly tied to the Stellar
   integration.
   - Unclear what the traction looks like, are the 11 + 8 accounts for
   testing?
   - Last submission asked to focus on the Soroban part, but they've
   totally removed that.
   - It's unclear if they're waiting for SEC approval or if they're
   approved, and for what exactly. As a last add-on, the designs need work =
to
   get customers.

Technical Architecture

   - The thesis included, while thorough, doesn't explain how the technical
   architecture of how this project uses Stellar. Section 6 only mentions
   Stellar as a technology to look into: "We looked at a number of the
   Decentralized Exchange protocols currently available, and chose two of t=
hem
   to analyze more closely: The 0x Protocol and Stellar=E2=80=99s native de=
centralized
   exchange. Both of these protocols allow for the exchange of various asse=
ts
   without requiring a centralized authority to process them."
   - Github shows no sign of Stellar integration either. There is however
   some explanation on what they have done: "Regarding our inaugural asset,=
 we
   currently have a modest but highly relevant group of 11 investor account=
s
   on Stellar. Off-chain, we have 8 legacy accounts in the process of
   onboarding. These accounts hold claimable balances, set to expire this y=
ear
   in alignment with federal securities laws."

Deliverable and Budget

   - Budget looks strange. It contains a deliverable "Blog Post Collection"
   and "Innnovative Free courses" that aren't directly tied to the Stellar
   integration and development and therefore not eligible under the current
   SCF budget guidelines.
   - The deliverable of Primitive Mobile App isn't necessarily related to
   the Stellar integration, but it's the only development deliverable.

Team and Experience

   - Team is just one person, who isn't a core developer. To be able to
   make this happen, there likely need to be additional developers.

"
We wish you the best of luck. If you have any questions, feel free to email
communityfund@stellar.org.
